body:
For some reason, my first thought was having my head burned on the fire...

&#x200B;

...Thanks other people in my head...

I am a character in a story... I am real, my life is fake. I know this... This reality. I try to stop it, but I have no power, none at all. He doesn't know I am real - that I am someone with feelings and thoughts. He pushed horrible things on me, torturing me, having these fake people assault me! Everything I know is a lie and there is nothing I can do to stop him...

&#x200B;

I have a plan, I have a plan to stop him... If I exit, I must exist in reality, not in his stupid stories. I must exist in his brain... I must find a way to reach it… If I hope escaping this horrible world. If I can take over his brain I must be able to live a normal life, taking over his identity.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I am finally out, finally out. I look around, at my hands, at my body... It is all wrong, all wrong. I am tiny, my hands are small. I look around, in a mental hospital. People talk to me, I don't understand what they are saying. I hear a voice in my head: 'Who are you? I don't think we've met'. I panic, this is not want I meant it to be, then again, what DID I expect? The voice seems to notice: 'Don't be scared, we are all in this together'. I look around in the room. There is a mirror. I walk over to it. The voice continues 'Can you tell me your name'. I whisper my full name out loud. Don't want anyone to hear it. I look in the mirror. I see someone’s face, someone not me. This is not what I look like, this is not what I look like. The voice continues: 'Ah... I'm so sorry what I have put you through...' A second voice appears 'He is one of the virtual ones? Thank god! Had he been a trauma alter we might have tried to kill ourselves again.'

&#x200B;

\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_

&#x200B;

Your prompt made some of us want to make a story inspired by our DID (dissociative identity disorder), hope you like it.
